// Adaptive Sorting Algorithm Implementation
// This program implements a sorting algorithm that can be evolved to adapt to different data patterns



// EVOLVE-BLOCK-START
// HYPOTHESIS-1: Switching to introsort (quicksort + heapsort fallback + insertion sort for small slices) will raise performance_score while keeping correctness.
// MECHANISM-1: Median-of-three pivot reduces bad partitions; depth limit prevents O(n^2); insertion sort is faster for tiny partitions.
// EXPECT-1: performance_score > 0.98
// RESULT-1: CONFIRMED (actual=0.998379753459225)
// HYPOTHESIS-2: Removing unused helpers and verbose comments will improve score by reducing code-length penalty (>500 chars).
